<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portoviejo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1535</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Portoviejo is the capital of Manabí province on the coast of Ecuador. It was founded by the Spanish in 1535 in the lands of the Manteño people, making it one of the oldest Spanish towns in the country. The city was heavily damaged by the earthquake of April 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portoviejo.jpg" alt="Portoviejo" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David C. S. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collage_Portoviejo.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
